.6 (BUDGET-SOFT-ROUTE-1, issue 1780). 0.23.2 was: // 0.23.2 CRON-ONLY-HEARTBEAT-1 (agent_issues 2397, pillar autonomy): each hourly scheduled run ends with a qnfo-audit fleet_heartbeat upsert (ok=0 when generation threw); write errors are logged. // 0.23.1 Q08-NAME-COMPOUND-1 + Q08-COMPOSE-TRAIL-1 (each writer's gate result is kept in q08_reader_tests): in a hyphenated compound only the capitalised parts are checked as names ("AI-driven", "Claude-generated"; run 386). 0.23.0 0.23.0 Q08-TECH-SYSTEMS-1: the analysis explains the technical system (components, data flow, the design decision or constraint behind the event, the trade-off) instead of an incentive template; the background reads full Wikipedia articles on the technologies; both reader prompts judge technical understanding. 0.22.1 0.22.1 Q08-PRUNE-FLOOR-2: the prune floor is the publish floor (3000 characters with title and verdict), so the repair stops instead of eroding a draft that can no longer publish (run 385). 0.22.0 0.22.0 Q08-WRITER-UPGRADE-1: kimi-k2.6 writes first with thinking off, nemotron and gpt-oss as per-request fallback. 0.21.0 0.21.0 Q08-FINAL-READ-1 + Q08-SOURCE-DEPTH-1 (eight comments and arXiv abstracts up to 3000 characters; the fact-checkers count background and comments as source): the exact text that would be published needs 2800 characters of body and a final two-family reader panel (vacuity-focused prompt, mean 4, no judge under 3, fails closed) after the fact check and its prunes. 0.20.3 0.20.3 Q08-ANALYSIS-CONCRETE-1: an analysis-check item counts only when the sentence it quotes has a digit, a quotation or a name; abstract reasoning flagged against the reviewers' own instruction is dropped (run 383). 0.20.2 0.20.2 Q08-VERDICT-NORM-1: near-miss verdict lines are normalised, and a first draft whose only problem is the verdict line gets the verdict micro-call (which now reads the essay) before a full rewrite (run 382). 0.20.1 0.20.1 Q08-MARK-SHIFT-1: an analysis marker placed where