f the body, and the marker never reaches readers or the published page. // 0.18.2 (run 375): "README", "CHANGELOG", "GitHub" and "repository" are not names the grounding check needs in the source (the source of a repository piece is its README); the fact revision is told to keep a news lede naming the subject and where it appeared. // 0.18.1 Q08-LEDE-PRUNE-1: the fact-check prune never deletes sentences of the first paragraph (a piece was published opening "Users therefore trust ..." after its lede was pruned); a flagged claim in the lede sends the draft to the model revision, and every pruned draft is re-checked with ledeProblems. // 0.18.0 Q08-CONTEXT-1 (owner 2026-10-13: "totally lacking in context and big-picture systems analysis"): each essay gets a BACKGROUND pack of verified reference text (Wikipedia lead sections for the story's subject and recent news coverage) that the writer may cite and the fact-check verifies against; the directive requires a context section and a systems analysis (parties, incentives, constraints, feedback loop, who gains and who pays, where else it operates); the fact-check treats framed analysis that adds no new name, number or event as not a violation, and a reviewer reason calling an item analysis marks it reasoning; readers cap a piece that only retells its source at 3. // 0.17.6 Q08-PRUNE-VERDICT-1 (run 369): the sentence prune sets the verdict line aside and puts it back unchanged, so a verdict that shared a paragraph with the last sentence is no longer damaged into a "missing verdict" failure. // 0.17.5 Q08-LEDE-SPLIT-1 (run 368): an overlong first paragraph is split at a sentence boundary into a lede of at most 70 words and a following paragraph, instead of failing "lede too long"; nothing is added or removed. // 0.17.4 Q08-TICK-BUDGET-1 (agent_issues 2479): an essay after a failed forecast waits for the next tick when more than 240 s are used (run 366 left no row: forecast 256 s + essay up to 644 s reached the 15-minute limit