ne floor, not the 2800-character writing floor (it rewrites an already pruned or edited draft), so a phrase-level tell is repaired instead of failing with "too short". // 0.15.0 Q08-READER-CUTS-1 (runs 339-355): the paragraph cuts the readers name ("delete paragraphs 4, 6 and 7", "cut the last two paragraphs") are applied deterministically before the model editor, at most half the body and only when the result passes the editor gate; the model editor is the fallback. // 0.14.11 Q08-FLOOR-PARAS-1 (run 354): a pruned or edited draft held to its lower floor needs 4 substantial paragraphs, not the 6 of a full 2800-character draft. // 0.14.10 Q08-PRUNE-FUZZY-1 (run 353): an unsupported item the reviewer paraphrased instead of quoting removes the one sentence sharing most of its content words (at least 4 and 60%), instead of "prune located nothing". // 0.14.9 Q08-TITLE-CARRY-2 (run 352): the title carry (editor drafts and the fact revision) uses every title rule of the gate (label, formula and Title Case titles), not only the dry-title pattern and the length limit. // 0.14.8 Q08-PRUNE-ROUNDS-2 + Q08-PARAPHRASE-1 (run 350): fact repair runs up to 8 rounds while it has used under 6 minutes (5 before), and a reviewer reason that only objects to the wording ("not in source as a direct quote", "not verbatim") marks a paraphrase, not a FACT; "not entirely in source" is read as a negation (it was read as support since 0.14.2). // 0.14.7 Q08-FACT-REVISION-FORMAT-1 (run 349): the fact revision keeps the draft's passing title and verdict line and gets the deterministic framing repair on a phrase-level-only gate failure, instead of failing on a label title it wrote. // 0.14.6 Q08-FACT-SHAPE-2 (runs 347-348): a reviewer item labelled FACT whose quoted text has no digit, quotation or capitalised name and uses generalising wording (wherever, any, every, if, therefore, would, could, pattern, mechanism, incentive) is reasoning; a plain modal claim stays a FACT. // 0.14.5 also removes the