T findings fail a draft (unlabelled ones count as FACT), INFERENCE findings are deleted when the draft can spare them; runs 333-335 failed only because reviewers listed the essay's own reasoning next to real fact errors. // 0.13.0 FRAMING-REPAIR-1 + FACTCHECK-DEGRADE-1 (agent_issues 2284, 2286, 2288; pillar reach): a gate failure made only of phrase-level tells is repaired without a model call (the flagged sentences removed, full gate re-run, at most a quarter of the sentences; logged as framing_repair rows and in the run error), the writer, editor and forecaster prompts carry one line naming the framing idioms the gate rejects, the retry feedback shows each flagged phrase in its sentence, and the fact-check panel tries every non-writer family on Workers AI (the writer families join the pool, cheaper sibling first) before a draft fails as unavailable. // 0.12.0 Q08-EDGE-CACHE-1 (issue 2343, pillar reach): plain GET pages are served from the edge cache for their public max-age=300 (TTFB 0.8-1.6 s measured: every view rendered from D1); a cache hit on a piece page still counts both reads; every HTML response carries Referrer-Policy and Permissions-Policy. // 0.11.19 Q08-READER-NOTHINK-1 (issue 2085): reader judges use the measured per-model reasoning switches and a 6000-token budget (2000 left reasoning judges without a verdict on 11 panel reads in 3 days). // 0.11.18 Q08-EDIT-FLOOR-1: the editor pass applies the readers' cuts and is held to 1800 characters, not the 2800-character writing floor (runs 319, 323, 327: readers asked to delete restating paragraphs, the editor was told to keep 2800 characters, the second panel rejected the same padding); forecasts keep the writing floor. // 0.11.17 Q08-PRUNE-FLOOR-1: a draft repaired by deleting the reviewers' quoted sentences is held to a 1500-character floor (the audit-repair floor), not the 2800-character writing floor, so the repair stops falling back to a model revision that writes new unsupported detail (runs 292-332: no piece since 2026-10-10 06:05); five prune rounds, one model revision at most, and the repair trail is kept in the run error. // 0.11.16 SINGLE-LETTER-1: a single capital letter (the O of O(n), a variable, a list label) is never read as a name by the grounding check (run 330: accuracy "name not in the source: O"). // 0.11.15 Q08-FACT-REPAIR-1 + FACTCHECK-NOTHINK-1 (issue 2349) + Q08-VERDICT-TOLERANT-1: reviewers run with reasoning off where a measured switch exists (0.7-2.6 s instead of 4-9 s), 75 s timeout, and a verdict is read from the explicit fields when the JSON is wrapped or truncated. // 0.11.13 Q08-PRUNE-1: a draft that fails the fact-check is first repaired by deleting exactly the sentences the reviewers quoted (deletion cannot add a fact; runs 319-326 show every model revision reintroducing unsupported detail), then re-verified in full, up to three rounds; a model revision is only the fallback. // 0.11.12 Q08-EDITOR-PHRASE-REVISE-1: an editor draft rejected only for phrase-level tells (a label title) gets one targeted revision instead of failing the run. 0.11.11 0.11.11 GROUND-HYPHEN-1: the name check treats unicode hyphens as "-" and a hyphenated source name grants its parts, and the capital/cost/policy-driven label-title pattern no longer rejects sentence-case titles (run 318: 'Capital-driven polishing eclipses the original creator'). // 0.11.8 Q08-GENERAL-CLAIMS-1: the writer states general mechanisms only as conditional reasoning from the source (run 315: "many programs assume", "the only reliable safeguard" were flagged as unsupported prevalence claims), and the reviewers do not count conditionals or mentions of the source as violations. // 0.11.7 Q08-FACTCHECK-POOL-1: fact-check reviewers run in a fixed order, llama-3.3-70b and qwen3-30b first, because the rotating pool led with models that timed out or exhausted their token budget (runs 305-314 ended fact-check unavailable). // 0.11.6 Q08-RICH-SOURCE-1: candidates are chosen for source richness (story, discussion and fetched article of at least 2200 characters, arXiv papers read from their HTML rendering) before writing starts, because the fact-check rejected every draft a thin source forced the writer to invent (run 314: unsupported claims about a story whose article could not be fetched); the richest candidate is used when none reaches the bar. // 0.11.5 Q08-PANEL-THRESHOLD-1: the reader panel passes at a mean of 3.5 with at least half the readers reading to the end (was 4 from both: readers splitting 3 and 4 rejected every source-only draft); the name check skips all-caps acronyms of up to five letters (the two-family fact-check still reviews them) and sentence-opening prepositions. // 0.11.4 Q08-AI-OBJECT-REPLY-1: Workers AI returns `response` as a parsed object when a model replies with bare JSON (llama, qwen), which became "[object Object]" and no verdict (run 312: three of five fact-check reviewers); every reply is now normalised to text before it is parsed. // 0.11.3 Q08-EDITOR-GROUNDED-1: the editor pass said "cut anything that only restates" with a 2800-character floor and "replace abstractions with people doing things", so thin-source drafts came back too short or invented concrete detail; the editor now adds nothing outside the draft and source and keeps the floor, the reader prompts ask for cuts never outside facts, the length label is 450-1100 words (700 words could never fit the 2800-character floor), and the editor-gate failure names its gate problems. // 0.11.2 Q08-FACTCHECK-DIAG-1: fact-check reviewers run one at a time over every non-writer family and a failure keeps its cause in the run error (the verdict outage had no visible reason). // 0.11.1 Q08-FACTCHECK-BUDGET-1: reviewers get 8000 tokens (2000 left reasoning models without a verdict, so every run ended "fact-check unavailable"); the name check ignores sentence connectives, compass adjectives and common technical acronyms. // 0.11.0 Q08-YIELD-REPAIR-1 (pillar: reach; owner directive 2026-10-11, automation must run user-free): generation runs hourly and audit/repair has its own :30 cron; an essay that fails the audit is repaired (unsupported claims deleted, correction note) before it is retracted and earlier audit retractions get one restoration attempt; essay length follows the source (450-1100 words, never padded) so the panel stops rejecting padding; name check ignores initials; article fetch upgrades http to https; attempt cap 4x. // 0.10.2 Q08-RENDER-1 + NO-ZENODO-DOI-2 (pillar: reach; owner directives 2026-10-10, agent_issues 2279 and 2275): titles, headings, list items, claims and previews render inline Markdown (*italic*, **bold**, `code`, links) and math (\\( \\), $$ $$, and $...$ only with a TeX token and no space inside, never before a digit, so currency stays literal) through q08Inline; <title>, og/twitter, citation meta, JSON-LD, RSS, e-mail digest, social text and BibTeX/RIS use q08Plain (markers stripped, TeX as Unicode); mdToHtml gains numbered lists and block quotes; the funnel copy no longer claims a DOI; the writer prompt states the title format. // 0.10.1 generative prompts name no example nouns (process and style only); 0.10.0 Q08-VERIFY-1 (pillar: reach, owner directive 2026-10-10: q08 content is 100% accurate and fact-checked): the writer prompts no longer ask for history from memory; a piece is published only when every name, year and figure is in its source material (signal plus the fetched article) and two reviewers from other model families find no unsupported claim (a reviewer outage fails closed); published pieces are re-audited each cron and a failure is retracted in public (410 notice, /retractions, out of index, feed, sitemap, APIs and social; forecasts built on it too). // 0.9.0 Q08-FORECAST-1 (pillar: reach): forecast mode. Every FORECAST_EVERY pieces the engine writes a most-likely scenario narrative from a published essay's mechanism (dated causal sequence, rival scenarios with probabilities, leading indica